### Start-of-let record

A start-of-let record logs each room’s state as a let starts: walls, floors, doors, glass, taps, oven, keys, and meter reads. Add dated photos.

At end of a let, compare the record and photos. Such a record helps show any harm beyond normal wear.

### Who holds copies

Landlord holds a master copy. Tenant gets a full copy at handover. An agent may hold a copy too. Have tenant add a date and a mark on each copy.

### What makes one weak at court

A court may see weak proof where:

- no date or dated photos;
- vague words, such as “good”;
- no room-by-room account;
- no key count or meter read;
- tenant lacks a copy;
- log made well after handover; or
- later changes lack dates and a clear note.
